#!/opt/homebrew/opt/lua@5.4/bin/lua
--
-- Pinned to lua@5.4 rather than `/usr/bin/env lua`, which follows whatever
-- Homebrew's unversioned `lua` formula happens to be. That formula moved from
-- 5.4 to 5.5, and the jump breaks the bar in two ways at once:
--
--   * lua-cjson and luaposix (required by aerospace.lua) live in the versioned
--     tree /opt/homebrew/lib/lua/5.4, which a 5.5 interpreter never searches --
--     hence "module 'cjson' not found" out of nowhere, with nothing uninstalled.
--   * SbarLua's sketchybar.so is compiled against the 5.4 C API, and loading it
--     into 5.5 kills the process outright instead of raising a lua error.
--
-- Upgrading the whole stack means rebuilding SbarLua from source and finding a
-- luaposix that builds on 5.5, so pin instead. lua@5.4 is keg-only, so this path
-- is stable and does not fight the unversioned formula. install.sh installs it
-- and targets luarocks at it explicitly.

